course: dictionary
lesson: 8690
title: Seize and its meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Seize» is a strong, formal word. It means to take hold of something suddenly and firmly. Everyday words for the same action are «grab» and «take». Use the sentence around it to choose the right meaning.
explain: «The whole party jumps up to seize him» tells you what happens next. They want to catch him quickly, so seize means grab. Try your meaning in the sentence: if «grab» still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
explain: «Seize» has more than one meaning, so check the context each time. A army can seize a town by force. Police can seize stolen goods by law. A child can seize a chance quickly. Each time, ask: what is being taken, and how?
fact: «Seize» means to take hold of something suddenly and firmly.
fact: «Seize» can mean to take control of a place by force, as in «Portugal seized the port of Malacca in 1511».
fact: When police or officials seize things, they take them away by law, as in «Police seized the stolen goods».
fact: «Seize the day» means to take a chance quickly.
fact: «Seize up» means to become stuck and stop working, like an engine with no oil.
exercise: In the story, the whole party jumps up to seize the Toad. What does seize mean here? | Sit down quietly | Wave to him gently | *Grab him suddenly and firmly | Thank him for a lovely ride
exercise: «Police seized the stolen goods.» What does seize mean here? | *To take the goods away by law | To give the goods back to the owner | To hide the goods under a bed | To buy the goods in a shop
exercise: The old engine has no oil, so it has stopped working and become stuck. Which word fits? | climbed | *seized up | danced | sang
test: «Portugal seized the port of Malacca in 1511.» What does seize mean here? | To sell fish at the port | To paint the port | *To take control of the port by force | To visit the port on holiday
test: Which word is closest in meaning to seize? | Forgive | Sleep | Whisper | *Grab
exam: What does «Seize the day» tell you to do? | Stop working until tomorrow | *Take a chance quickly | Sleep late and wait | Write a long letter
